IntentRouter_Constructor
├── it should deploy shortcuts executed only by the router
└── it should expose the EIP-712 domain

IntentRouter_ExecuteIntent
├── when the caller is not the keeper
│   └── it should revert with NotKeeper
├── when the chain id does not match
│   └── it should revert with WrongChain
├── when executed before start
│   └── it should revert with TooEarly
├── when executed after the deadline
│   └── it should revert with Expired
├── when the signature is not the owner's
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
├── when the intent is tampered after signing
│   └── it should revert with InvalidSignature
├── when the nonce was already used
│   └── it should revert with NonceUsed
├── when the nonce was cancelled
│   └── it should revert with NonceUsed
├── when the owner is a contract wallet
│   └── it should accept an ERC-1271 signature
├── when the owner has code but signs with its key
│   └── it should accept the ECDSA signature
├── when the keeper supplies the route
│   ├── it should pull tokensIn from the owner into shortcuts
│   ├── it should run the keeper's route
│   ├── it should measure the delta at the recipient
│   ├── it should consume the nonce
│   └── it should emit IntentExecuted
├── when the route is committed
│   ├── it should run the committed route and ignore the keeper's bytes
│   └── it should execute without an outcome floor
├── when the committed route misses the floor
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when the keeper supplies the route and tokensOut is empty
│   └── it should revert with Unconstrained
├── when a minimum is zero
│   └── it should revert with Unconstrained
├── when the delta is below the minimum
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when any tokenOut misses its minimum
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow
├── when the recipient balance decreases
│   └── it should revert with AmountTooLow, not a Panic
├── when tokenOut is native
│   └── it should measure the native delta at the recipient
├── when the outcome is a minted NFT
│   └── it should satisfy the count minimum with whatever id arrived
├── when the outcome is an ERC1155
│   └── it should measure the id balance at the recipient
├── when tokenIn is native
│   └── it should revert with UnsupportedTokenType
├── when tokenIn is an NFT
│   └── it should pull the committed tokenId from the owner
├── when tokenIn is an ERC1155
│   └── it should pull the committed amount of the id from the owner
├── when the owner has not approved
│   └── it should revert on the pull
├── when the intent fee is set
│   ├── it should pull the fee from the owner to the keeper
│   └── it should ignore the refund fee
├── when the intent fee is native
│   └── it should revert with UnsupportedTokenType
├── when the keeper is zero
│   └── it should let any caller execute and pay them the fee
├── when the route reverts
│   └── it should bubble the revert
└── when a shortcut reenters executeIntent
    └── it should revert with ReentrancyGuardReentrantCall

IntentRouter_Cancel
├── when the owner cancels a nonce
│   ├── it should mark the nonce used
│   ├── it should emit IntentCancelled
│   └── it should leave other nonces and owners untouched
└── when the nonce is already used
    └── it should revert with NonceUsed

IntentRouter_Hash
└── when hashed against the reference encoder
    ├── it should match the ethers TypedDataEncoder digest
    └── it should compose the domain from the exposed EIP-712 fields
